# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: MarionOrVargaPath

translate es strings:

    old "It was more than two weeks after the victory over the eastern tribesmen, when Sarah arrived early for a council meeting, surprised to find the room already full."
    new "Fue más de dos semanas después de la victoria sobre los tribus del este, cuando Sarah llegó temprano a una reunión del consejo, sorprendida al encontrar la sala ya llena."

    old "There was a busy chatter, which suddenly felt silent as everyone noticed Sarah."
    new "Hubo un bullicioso murmullo que de repente se sintió en silencio cuando todos notaron a Sarah."

    old "Thomas was sitting back in this throne, waiving at Sarah excitedly as she approached."
    new "Thomas se recostaba en ese trono, saludando a Sarah con entusiasmo mientras ella se acercaba."

    old "Sarah had almost reached the table, when suddenly, Marion stood up."
    new "Sarah había llegado casi a la mesa cuando de repente Marion se puso de pie."

    old "Sarah saw Thomas suppress laughter. In between his laughs he managed to speak."
    new "Sarah vio cómo Thomas contenía la risa. Entre carcajada y carcajada logró hablar."

    old "I believe our honorable friend, Marion, has something he wanted to say to you."
    new "Creo que nuestro honorable amigo Marion tiene algo que decirte."

    old "Sarah could feel a pit in her stomach."
    new "Sarah sentía un nudo en el estómago."

    old "She feared she already knew what he was planning to do."
    new "Temía que ya supiera qué planeaba hacer."

    old "Confused, Sarah stared at Marion."
    new "Confundida, Sarah lo miró con asombro."

    old "Marion fell to one knee, and extended a hand, holding a small box carved out of oak."
    new "Marion se arrodilló y extendió la mano, sosteniendo una pequeña caja tallada en roble."

    old "Sarah Rose, having given it serious consideration, I wish to pronounce in front of all these people, my love for you."
    new "Sarah Rose, tras darle una seria consideración, deseo pronunciar ante todas estas personas mi amor por ti."

    old "Please give me the honour of your hand, and I will swear to always be true."
    new "Por favor, concédeme el honor de tu mano y yo juraré ser siempre fiel."

    old "Stunned, Sarah felt it almost physically difficult to remain standing."
    new "Atónita, Sarah sintió que era casi físicamente imposible mantenerse de pie."

    old "The edges of her vision seemed to blur, and the ground under her feet began to shift."
    new "Los bordes de su visión parecían desenfocarse, y el suelo bajo sus pies comenzó a desplazarse."

    old "Accept Marion's proposal."
    new "Aceptar la propuesta de Marion."

    old "Yes."
    new "Sí."

    old "The words seemed to slip out before she had given it any thought."
    new "Las palabras parecieron escapar antes de que ella pudiera pensar en ellas."

    old "She saw the faces around the table, clearly, she was not alone in her surprised."
    new "Vio las caras que había alrededor de la mesa, y claramente no era la única sorprendida."

    old "Still on his knees, she saw Marion's face beaming."
    new "Aún de rodillas, vio la cara de Marion brillar."

    old "She watched as he rose to his feet, grabbed her by the waist and spun her around."
    new "La observó mientras se ponía de pie, la agarraba por la cintura y la giraba."

    old "All around the room, people began to give their congratulations to the new couple."
    new "Por todas partes de la habitación, la gente comenzó a ofrecer sus felicitaciones a la nueva pareja."

    old "Varga was the only one who carried a pained expression on his face."
    new "Varga era el único que llevaba una expresión de dolor en su rostro."

    old "Sarah watched it all unfold as if this was happening to someone else."
    new "Sarah observaba cómo todo se desarrollaba como si estuviera ocurriendo a alguien más."

    old "Reject Marion's proposal."
    new "Rechazar la propuesta de Marion."

    old "Suddenly, Sarah felt all the emotions of the shock pushed out and she found her footing again."
    new "De repente, Sarah sintió que todas las emociones del shock fueron expulsadas y recuperó el equilibrio."

    old "Rage was now keeping her tethered."
    new "La rabia la mantenía ahora atada."

    old "In only two broad steps she closed the distance between herself and Marion, standing over the imbecile as he was still kneeling."
    new "En solo dos amplios pasos cerró la distancia entre sí y Marion, alzándose sobre el imbécil mientras aún estaba de rodillas."

    old "A more humble man would have seen the signs of what came next, but Marion was not humble."
    new "Un hombre más humilde habría visto las señales de lo que venía a continuación, pero Marion no era humilde."

    old "A shattering crack rang out across the room, followed by a deafening silence."
    new "Un crujido desgarrador resonó por la habitación, seguido de un silencio ensordecedor."

    old "Marion's face was frozen off to the side, unable to process the slap, either physically or emotionally."
    new "El rostro de Marion estaba congelado hacia un lado, incapaz de procesar el azote, ya sea físicamente o emocionalmente."

    old "Sarah could see from the corners of her eyes that everyone was staring at her."
    new "Sarah podía ver desde los rincones de sus ojos que todos la miraban."

    old "Marriage?"
    new "¿Matrimonio?"

    old "Are you insane?"
    new "¿Estás loca?"

    old "We were nothing more than friends at best, Marion."
    new "Solo éramos amigos, en el mejor de los casos, Marion."

    old "I never gave you my blessing, I never agreed to any of this."
    new "Nunca te di mi bendición, nunca acepté ninguno de esto."

    old "And if you thought I would feel forced to say yes because we were in public, you're as big of an idiot as you are craven."
    new "Y si pensabas que me sentiría forzada a decir que sí porque estábamos en público, eres tan idiota como eres cobarde."

    old "The only thing you've managed to do today is humiliate me, and make a joke of yourself."
    new "Lo único que has logrado hacer hoy es humillarme y burlarte de ti mismo."

    old "Marion was now crawling away from her, trying to recover and get back on his feet."
    new "Marion ahora se arrastraba alejándose de ella, intentando recuperarse y volver a ponerse de pie."

    old "By the time he had gotten onto his feet, Sarah could see his face had turned bright red."
    new "Sarah pudo ver que su rostro se había puesto de un rojo intenso apenas logró ponerse de pie."

    old "I brought it up with Thomas...he thought it would be..."
    new "Lo comenté con Thomas... él pensó que sería..."

    old "A joke, Marion. He probably thought you were a joke, and I suppose, in that regard, he was right."
    new "Una broma, Marion. Probablemente pensó que eras una broma, y supongo que, en ese sentido, tenía razón."

    old "I don't want to see you here ever again. You're off the council."
    new "No quiero verte aquí nunca más. Estás desterrada."

    old "Leave, and pray that nobody ever hears how much you humiliated yourself today."
    new "Déjame y ruega que nadie escuche cuánto te has humillado hoy."

    old "Marion searched for words, but unable to find any, turned around and stormed off."
    new "Marion buscó palabras, pero no encontró ninguna, así que dio la vuelta y se marchó con rabia."

    old "Sarah snapped back to the table full of advisors."
    new "Sarah volvió a sí misma ante la mesa llena de consejeros."

    old "Her eyes ran across all the faces. Most were a mix of stunned and mortified, there was only one exception."
    new "Sus ojos recorrieron todos los rostros. La mayoría eran una mezcla de atónitos y avergonzados; solo había una excepción."

    old "Varga was brightly smiling, clearly having enjoyed the humiliation of Marion."
    new "Varga sonreía con una alegría evidente, disfrutando claramente de la humillación que había infligido a Marion."

    old "If I find out any of you set him up to this, I swear you're going to pay for it."
    new "Si descubro que alguno de ustedes lo metió en esto, juro que pagarán con su vida."

    old "Sarah herself now turned around and stormed off, in no mood to continue the council meeting."
    new "Sarah ahora se dio la vuelta y salió a trompicones, sin ánimo de continuar la reunión del consejo."
